### Ramailo Pokhara API seed file
### Compatible with the VS Code REST Client extension / JetBrains HTTP Client.
### IMPORTANT: This creates DEMO content. Review/edit it before using it as real news.
### Run requests from top to bottom. Category creation is intended for a fresh database.

@baseUrl = http://localhost:3000
@adminEmail = admin@example.com
@adminPassword = CHANGE_ME

### 1) Health check
GET {{baseUrl}}/

### 2) Get NextAuth CSRF token
# @name csrf
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/auth/csrf
Accept: application/json

### 3) Sign in as admin
### REST Client normally keeps the session cookie for subsequent requests.
# @name login
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/auth/callback/credentials
Content-Type: application/x-www-form-urlencoded
Accept: application/json

csrfToken={{csrf.response.body.$.csrfToken}}&email={{adminEmail}}&password={{adminPassword}}&callbackUrl={{baseUrl}}/admin&redirect=false&json=true

### 4) Confirm authenticated session
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/auth/session
Accept: application/json

